\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Federal Contractors Must Pay $15 Wage\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 288 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 April 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 President Biden signed an executive order Tuesday requiring that federal contractors pay a $15-an-hour minimum wage, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 The order affects hundreds of thousands of people working on federal contracts, the White House said, including cleaning and maintenance workers, as well as nursing assistants and food-service workers.\par \par \uc2 Under the order, starting Jan. 30, 2022, all agencies will need to include a $15 minimum wage in new contract solicitations, and by March 30, 2022, all agencies must implement it into new contracts. Agencies will also need to incorporate it into existing contracts when they are extended.\par \par \uc2 The current minimum wage for workers performing work on covered federal contracts is $10.95. The order also phases out the use of a tipped minimum wage for federal contractors, currently $7.65 an hour, by 2024.\par \par \uc2 In January, Mr. Biden signed an order to start the process so that he could sign this order within his first 100 days. At the time, the White House said he would sign an order requiring that federal contractors pay a $15-an-hour minimum wage and provide paid leave for their employees.\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official said that paid leave wasn't incorporated into this plan but noted that there are tax credits for employers in the recent Covid-19 aid bill that cover leave for certain coronavirus-related reasons.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden campaigned on a pledge to raise the federal minimum wage to $15 an hour. A push by Democrats to include the wage boost in the $1.9 trillion Covid-19 relief law was unsuccessful. The White House has said Mr. Biden remains committed to the goal.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210428eh4s00014\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
