\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  Prepares to Reopen Offices for Hybrid-Work Era\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kimberly Chin \par \uc2 549 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 March 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 ., one of the first American companies to ask staff to shift to remote work more than a year ago as the coronavirus pandemic hit, is ready to begin welcoming employees back to the office.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's Redmond, Wash., headquarters and nearby campuses will start shifting to a hybrid-work approach on March 29, with some employees returning to office desks while others work from home, the company said Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Our goal is to give employees further flexibility, allowing people to work where they feel most productive and comfortable, while also encouraging employees to work from home as the virus and related variants remain concerning," \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said in a blog post.\par \par \uc2 The software company's office locations spanning 21 countries will be ready to accommodate additional workers in compliance with guidance from local authorities, the company said. The initial guidance affects roughly 20% of \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's more than 160,000 employees, the company said.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said it doesn't expect to recall all employees soon. Once the pandemic is no longer a significant threat to communities, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said, the company expects a partial work-from-home schedule to be routine for many of its jobs. The company previously has said it would allow some workers to work remotely on a permanent basis with their manager's approval.\par \par \uc2 With the Covid-19 vaccine rollout progressing, the shift to hybrid work is shaping up to be a critical challenge for companies this year, not unlike last year's rush to figure out how to keep business going with employees scattered at home. Like last year, actions aren't uniform.\par \par \uc2 Many companies are still holding off on bringing workers back to the office. \uc2 Google\uc2  parent \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 . is keeping most of its staff working remotely until at least September. Social-media company \uc2 Twitter Inc\uc2 . said most of its staff would be able to keep working remotely after the pandemic has ended. \uc2 Facebook Inc\uc2 . has moved toward having a substantially larger portion of employees working remotely.\par \par \uc2 The number of Americans working from home has surged during the pandemic, and many corporate leaders expect that to continue. According to a global survey by \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  that was released on Monday, 73% of workers said they want flexible work-from-home policies to stay, and 65% of employees reported wanting more in-person time with their teams after the pandemic. About 66% of businesses were considering redesigning offices to accommodate hybrid work environments.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  is betting that the hybrid-work era will spawn a new wave of requirements to accommodate employees. The company posted a year of strong growth amid the pandemic, as companies adapted to navigate the remote-work environment and embraced the kind of cloud-computing services and workplace-collaboration tools the company sells.\par \par \uc2 Its videogaming business has enjoyed significant success among people stuck at home, and its Teams workplace-collaboration software also experienced large growth in user numbers.\par \par \uc2 Half of the company's workforce or more could take advantage of flexible work arrangements, Microsoft Chief Executive \uc2 Satya Nadella\uc2  said at The Wall Street Journal's CEO Council Summit.\par \par \uc2 Executives at other companies have cited challenges with training, integrating new employees and finishing projects with workers plugging away from their homes.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210323eh3n0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
