\par\par \b \uc2 LIRR Service Cuts Lead to Crowding\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Berger \par \uc2 598 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 March 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A8A\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Long Island Rail Road\uc2  enacted new service reductions on its trains Monday morning, leading to some rider complaints about overcrowding and concerns about a lack of social distancing for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The state-controlled \uc2 Metropolitan Transportation Authority\uc2 , which runs LIRR, said the new timetable reflects a 25% systemwide reduction. Service already had been cut by 20% because of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 State transportation officials say the schedule change reflects weekday ridership, which is about 75% lower than pre-pandemic levels as many white-collar employees have continued to work remotely.\par \par \uc2 Some commuters on Monday posted photographs and messages on social media asking how they were supposed to maintain social distancing when people are forced to sit or stand close together.\par \par \uc2 State \uc2 Sen. Todd Kaminsky\uc2 , a Long Island Democrat, said the crowding undermines New York's attempts to restore confidence in public transportation. "Making it unpleasant, undignified and a potentially unsafe experience does not make sense," he said.\par \par \uc2 Gerard Bringmann, chairman of the Long Island Rail Road Commuter Council, an advocacy group, said the reality is that now many riders had to wait 30 to 60 minutes between trains during the morning rush hour.\par \par \uc2 MTA\uc2  officials said the crowding wasn't as bad as social media made it appear.\par \par \uc2 Phil Eng, the president of LIRR, said 77% of rush-hour trains were less than half full and that crowding was limited to a few services or was isolated to certain cars.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Eng said the railroad will add one train on each of the Ronkonkoma and Babylon branches Tuesday morning and add cars to one train on the Long Beach Branch to alleviate crowding.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Eng also urged riders to check the LIRR TrainTime app, which uses weight sensors to tell riders how full each car is before a train arrives.\par \par \uc2 The state-controlled \uc2 MTA\uc2 , which also runs Metro-North Railroad and New York City's subway and bus systems, has lost billions of dollars during the coronavirus pandemic because of a drop in revenue from fares and taxes.\par \par \uc2 The authority, which was in a fiscal crisis before the pandemic, has received $8 billion in federal relief so far. It expects to receive a further $6.5 billion in the Biden administration's latest Covid-19 relief bill. Yet, it still needs to reduce costs to balance its almost $18 billion operating budget.\par \par \uc2 Metro-North Railroad, which has recovered more slowly than LIRR, is running 63% of its pre-pandemic service. \uc2 MTA\uc2  officials are debating whether to reduce service on the subway, which currently has a ridership of 70% below normal levels.\par \par \uc2 MTA\uc2  officials estimate the new LIRR timetable will save about $16 million in annual running costs. Mr. Eng said the service reductions will save millions more by giving track workers more time to perform daytime repairs and upgrades to the LIRR system.\par \par \uc2 MTA\uc2  officials have emphasized that trains and buses have good ventilation and are safe during. But researchers are still trying to discern the risk of infection from an airborne virus, especially as the region reopens.\par \par \uc2 Joshua Stein, a healthcare attorney, returned to commuting on the LIRR from Valley Stream to his office in Manhattan in September.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Stein, who is 36 years old, said his trains have been getting progressively busier, but he felt comfortable until Monday morning, when his car became more crowded than usual.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Stein said so many seats on his train were occupied that people chose to stand. "To me, a safe plan is having plenty of room in the cars," he said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210309eh390001e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
