\par\par \uc2 REVIEW & OUTLOOK (Editorial)\par \b \uc2 Plan B for a $15 Minimum Wage\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 March 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A16\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 As expected, the Senate's parliamentarian ruled last week that mandating a nationwide $15 minimum wage cannot be done via budget reconciliation, with a mere 51 votes. Some progressives, including some in Congress, are not eager to reconcile with this procedural flaw. "Replace the parliamentarian," Rep. Ilhan Omar tweeted. "This is unacceptable."\par \par \uc2 Rep. Ro Khanna's approach was in the same vein: "This is an advisory, not a ruling." He called on Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , as the Senate's constitutional leader, "to disregard and rule a $15 minimum wage in order." But doing so would mean the end, forever, of the longstanding Byrd rule, which governs reconciliation. President Biden, an institutionalist who gave a eulogy for the eponymous Senator Robert Byrd, seems unlikely to go for it. "He respects the parliamentarian's decision and the Senate's process," the White House press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 Hence the shift to Plan B. Senator Bernie Sanders said he would work on "an amendment to take tax deductions away from large, profitable corporations that don't pay workers at least $15 an hour." That idea, he insisted, "must be included in this reconciliation bill." Senator \uc2 Ron Wyden\uc2  said he wants "a 5 percent penalty on a big corporations' total payroll if any workers earn less than a certain amount."\par \par \uc2 But to sneak through reconciliation, any such provision would have to pass muster with the parliamentarian. One comparison is ObamaCare's mandate to buy health insurance or else pay a penalty. When the GOP pushed to kill it in 2015, "the Senate parliamentarian ruled that the bill's provisions to repeal the individual and employer mandates were extraneous," as the \uc2 Congressional Research Service\uc2  later put it. That's why the mandate remains law, though Republicans later cut its penalty to $0.\par \par \uc2 Even if the parliamentarian were swayed, passing a Plan B would require getting votes from Arizona's Kyrsten Sinema and West Virginia's Joe Manchin. Mr. Manchin thinks $15 an hour is too high. "Eleven dollars is the right place to be," he said recently.\par \par \uc2 How could he turn around and support the Sanders and Wyden plans? They'd hit big companies only, but they'd still increase the lunacy of treating the labor market in Harpers Ferry, W.Va., the same as the one in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 Ditto for Republican \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 's proposals. On Friday the Missouri Senator backed a $15 minimum wage for "companies with revenues of $1 billion." Earlier he floated a tax credit to send workers quarterly payments set at 50% of the difference between their wages and a baseline of $16.50 an hour.\par \par \uc2 This would be a subsidy tilted toward rural workers, especially, who would get more given their low cost of living. The whole city of Seattle would apparently be exempt, since its minimum wage is $16.69. Also, what does it do to initiative if a worker loses 50 cents of tax credits when he gets a $1 raise?\par \par \uc2 A federal wage mandate makes little sense in a country as large and economically diverse as the United States. Hawaii's overall prices run 119% of the national level, compared with 84% in Mississippi, per 2019 data from the \uc2 Bureau of Economic Analysis\uc2 . They're 135% of the national level in the San Francisco region, against very inexpensive rural areas in low-cost states.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  recently estimated that a $15 minimum wage would cost 1.4 million jobs. We realize that Mr. Hawley wants to be seen as a tribune of working people, but putting the least skilled out of work by adopting progressive economic policies isn't the way to do it.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210301eh310000n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
