\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Setback on $15 Minimum Strains Biden Ties With Left\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tarini Parti and Lindsay Wise \par \uc2 765 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 March 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A major setback last week to the administration's push for a $15 federal minimum wage could test President Biden's ability to keep Democrats united and shape his relationship with progressives.\par \par \uc2 Democrats attached the wage increase, one of Mr. Biden's 2020 campaign promises, to their $1.9 trillion Covid-19 relief package and sought to pass it under special rules that wouldn't require any Republican votes in the 50-50 Senate. The nonpartisan Senate parliamentarian determined that the minimum-wage increase didn't comply with those rules.\par \par \uc2 Progressive lawmakers and activists quickly called for Democrats to find a way around the ruling and raise the minimum wage, floating options such as overturning the parliamentarian's decision or abolishing the 60-vote threshold for most legislation in the Senate. Those moves are unlikely to succeed because they are opposed by some centrists in Mr. Biden's party, who also objected to including the minimum-wage increase in the Covid-19 bill and whose support the president needs to pass legislation in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The White House said Mr. Biden would follow the decision of the parliamentarian and seek to increase the minimum wage through another path. But the ruling is reviving a debate among Democrats over whether to break with recent precedent -- and institutional rules -- to make sweeping changes, such as ending the legislative filibuster or expanding the number of seats on the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 "In the end, it's gonna be about how are we going to deliver on the promises we made," said \uc2 Rep. Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (D., Wash.), co-chair of the Congressional Progressive Caucus. She said the party couldn't disappoint Democratic voters on the minimum-wage issue, especially in states such as Georgia and Arizona that Mr. Biden flipped in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Former Rep. Cedric Richmond, senior adviser to Mr. Biden, said the president would continue to push for raising the minimum wage. "We're going to find another way," he said.\par \par \uc2 The rift on the wage increase comes as some on the left have voiced criticism over the administration's handling of the rise in unaccompanied minors crossing the border, where many children are being held in Border Patrol custody longer than normally allowed. Some progressives have called for reorganizing the agencies that deal with migrants. And they are unhappy with Mr. Biden's recent comments that he wouldn't cancel $50,000 in student debt, as many progressives want, and an airstrike the president ordered in Syria without first consulting lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 While many in his party back the minimum-wage increase, most Republicans and some centrist Democrats, including Sens. Joe Manchin of West Virginia and Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona, have said they oppose the wage increase attached to the Covid-19 relief bill.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez (D., N.Y.) said she has kept in touch with White House chief of staff Ron Klain and believes the president is operating in good faith with progressives. She said Democrats should consider all options to get the proposed minimum wage through and that centrists like Mr. Manchin were the ones dividing the party.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Manchin's office didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Andrew Duehren and Eliza Collins contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Others Advocate\par \par \uc2 A Smaller Boost\par \par \uc2 Democratic Sen. Joe Manchin of West Virginia has called for a smaller increase in the federal minimum wage to $11 an hour, up from the current rate of $7.25 an hour.\par \par \uc2 Republican Sens. Tom Cotton of Arkansas and \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  of Utah have called for an hourly wage of $10.\par \par \uc2 Officials haven't said whether President Biden would support a smaller increase. He noted during a recent CNN town hall that a minimum-wage increase would be phased in over time.\par \par \uc2 "We need the president to use his forum, his bully pulpit to call out the cost of not doing this right now," said the Rev. William Barber, co-chairman of the Poor People's Campaign, which has been holding rallies and lobbying lawmakers on raising the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 Some outside groups are warning that failing to raise the minimum wage could hurt Democrats in the midterms and threaten the rest of Mr. Biden's agenda. "An issue like a $15 minimum wage, which was passed by a ballot measure in Florida even though Trump won that state in 2020, is exactly the kind of issue they need to deliver on," said Joseph Geevarghese, executive director of the progressive group Our Revolution.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210301eh310001j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
